        "en": "A long time! An oak can take 20 years or more just to make its own first acorns."
      },
      "src": [
        "rwn-oak"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "How do worms breathe?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Through their skin, which has to stay damp. They have no lungs."
      },
      "src": [
        "kg-ew"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Why do baby deer have spots?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "The spots help fawns hide in the forest. They fade at 3 to 5 months."
      },
      "src": [
        "mdc-wtd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Are bluebirds really blue?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Their feathers have no blue colour. Tiny cells reflect blue light, so they look blue."
      },
      "src": [
        "wbu-eb"
      ]
    }
